   Check if hdpx.so links to libasan

## Use valgrind instead:

2. Run tests:

  Interactive:
  ./R-valgrind
  # In R:
  devtools::load_all()
  # ... run your code ...
  q()  # Exit

  Automated test:
  ./R-valgrind < test-valgrind.R

  Quick test:
  ./R-valgrind -e 'devtools::load_all(); devtools::test()'

  3. View results:

  # Full report
  cat valgrind-hdpx.log

  # Just leak summary
  grep -A 20 'LEAK SUMMARY' valgrind-hdpx.log

  # Just errors
  grep -E '(definitely|indirectly) lost' valgrind-hdpx.log

  What to focus on:

  - Definitely lost: These are real leaks - must fix
  - Indirectly lost: Memory leaked because it was only referenced by "definitely lost" blocks
  - Still reachable: Memory not freed but still has pointers (often false positives from R internals - suppressed)
  - Possibly lost: May or may not be real leaks

  The custom valgrind-suppressions.supp file will filter out common R internal "leaks" so you can focus on real
  issues in your C code.